{{/* @dot donseba/go-webthings-docs/internal/website.DocsArticleData */}}
<article class="grid max-w-5xl gap-6">
    {{ template "hero.gohtml" . }}

<div class="callout">
    <strong>Configure during startup.</strong>
    <p>After the first request is served, registration freezes, also on routers mounted on it, to avoid runtime mutation races. Later registration panics, or returns an error through the <code>Try</code> APIs.</p>
</div>

<h2>Recommended defaults</h2>
<pre><code>r := router.NewSite()
r.UseAll(
    middleware.RequestID,
    middleware.RealIPWithOptions(middleware.RealIPOptions{
        TrustedProxies: []string{"127.0.0.1/32", "::1/128"},
    }),
    middleware.Logger(),
    middleware.Recover,
    // On every response, also the router's own redirects and plain 404s.
    middleware.SecurityHeaders(middleware.SecurityHeadersOptions{
        ContentTypeOptions: "nosniff",
        ReferrerPolicy:     "strict-origin-when-cross-origin",
    }),
)
r.Use(middleware.SecurityHeaders(middleware.SecurityHeadersOptions{FrameOptions: "DENY"})) // pages
r.Use(middleware.Timeout(10 * time.Second))                                                 // not around streaming routes
// routes ...

log.Fatal(http.ListenAndServe(":8080", r))</code></pre>

<h2>Before shipping</h2>
<ul class="docs-list">
    <li>Register routes only during startup.</li>
    <li>Prefer <code>Try*</code> registration if bootstrap should return explicit errors.</li>
    <li>Use <code>RealIPWithOptions</code> behind proxies, listing only your own proxies. <code>RealIP</code> trusts none.</li>
    <li>Register middleware before routes, since <code>Use</code> after routes panics, and use <code>UseAll</code> (or wrap the router) for middleware that must see every request.</li>
    <li>Set headers every response must carry, such as <code>X-Content-Type-Options</code>, with <code>UseAll</code>: <code>Use</code> middleware does not run for the router's own redirects and plain 404 and 405 answers.</li>
    <li>Create <code>Compress</code> with one or two levels: each level in use keeps up to <code>min(GOMAXPROCS, 16)</code> idle gzip writers of about 1 MB.</li>
    <li>Avoid response buffering middleware, such as <code>Timeout</code> and <code>ContentLengthMiddleware</code>, for streaming responses, and flush those explicitly.</li>
    <li>Run <code>go test ./...</code>, <code>go test -race ./...</code>, and <code>go vet ./...</code>.</li>
    <li>Add app-level tests for mounted routers, subdomains, and custom middleware.</li>
</ul>
</article>

